.* MAIN: the system main menu, where a session starts.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 3'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='MAIN'.
:IMPORT NAME=SIGNOFF PNLGRP=QHWMCMD.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='MENU INFO'.F13=Information Assistant
:KEYI KEY=F23 ACTION='RETURN 23'.F23=Set initial menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=MAIN HELP=HLPMAIN KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.QS/400 Main Menu
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='MENU USER' HELP='MAIN/OPT1'.User tasks
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='MENU OFCTSK' HELP='MAIN/OPT2'.Office tasks
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='MENU SYSTEM' HELP='MAIN/OPT3'.General system tasks
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='MENU DATA' HELP='MAIN/OPT4'.Files, libraries, and folders
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='MENU PROGRAM' HELP='MAIN/OPT5'.Programming
:MENUI OPTION=6 ACTION='MENU CMN' HELP='MAIN/OPT6'.Communications
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='MENU DEFINE' HELP='MAIN/OPT7'.Define or change the system
:MENUI OPTION=8 ACTION='MENU PROBLEM' HELP='MAIN/OPT8'.Problem handling
:MENUI OPTION=9 ACTION='MENU MAJOR' HELP='MAIN/OPT9'.Display a menu
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='MENU INFO' HELP='MAIN/OPT10'.Information Assistant options
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='MENU ACCESS' HELP='MAIN/OPT11'.QS/400 Access tasks
:MENUI OPTION=90 ACTION='CMD SIGNOFF' HELP=SIGNOFF.Sign off
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPMAIN.QS/400 Main Menu - Help
:P.The main menu is where a session begins: from it you reach the
menus of the system's tasks, or run a command directly.
:H2.Choosing an Option
:P.Type the number of an option on the line at the bottom and press
Enter. The menu the option names takes the place of this one; F12 on
it brings this menu back.
:P.To run a command instead, type it on the same line and press Enter.
F4 with nothing typed lists the command groups to choose from; F4
after a command name shows its parameters to fill in. F9 brings back
the command you ran last, to run it again or change it first.
:P.To show another menu, type GO and the menu's name, for example GO
MAJOR for the command groups. The name of the menu on the display is
in its upper left corner.
:H2.Function Keys
:P.F3 leaves the menu, signing off when it is the first one of the
session. F12 returns to the menu shown before this one. F13 shows the
Information Assistant options. F23 makes this menu the one your
sessions start with.
:H2.Signing Off
:P.Option 90 signs off. The SIGNOFF command does the same, and with
LOG(*LIST) keeps the session's job log as a spooled file.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Information Assistant
:PD.Shows menu INFO.
:PT.F23=Set initial menu
:PD.Set initial menu.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT1'.User tasks
:P.Option 1. Shows menu USER&colon. User tasks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT2'.Office tasks
:P.Option 2. Shows menu OFCTSK&colon. Office tasks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT3'.General system tasks
:P.Option 3. Shows menu SYSTEM&colon. General system tasks.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT4'.Files, libraries, and folders
:P.Option 4. Shows menu DATA&colon. Files, libraries, and folders.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT5'.Programming
:P.Option 5. Shows menu PROGRAM&colon. Programming.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT6'.Communications
:P.Option 6. Shows menu CMN&colon. Communications.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT7'.Define or change the system
:P.Option 7. Shows menu DEFINE&colon. Define or change the system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT8'.Problem handling
:P.Option 8. Shows menu PROBLEM&colon. Problem handling.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT9'.Display a menu
:P.Option 9. Shows menu MAJOR&colon. Display a menu.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT10'.Information Assistant options
:P.Option 10. Shows menu INFO&colon. Information Assistant options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='MAIN/OPT11'.QS/400 Access tasks
:P.Option 11. Shows menu ACCESS&colon. QS/400 Access tasks.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
